Stacks works on the principle of LIFO(Last In First Out).

Stacks basically has three operations:-
    1.Push:- Pushing the element to the top of Stack.
    2.Pop:- Taking out element from the top of Stack.
    3.Peek:- Returns the element present at the top of the Stack.

Stack Underflow:-
    When the stack is empty and we are popping or peeking an element, in this condition an error of Underflow arises.

Stack Overflow:-
    When the stack is full and we are pushing an element, in this condition an error of Overflow arises.